# njin-mail reverse proxy — every tenant webmail hostname (mail.<client-domain>)
# proxies to the same backend process on loopback. Caddy issues and renews a
# Let's Encrypt certificate per domain listed below automatically.
#
# IMPORTANT: never rewrite/override the Host header here. The app enforces
# multi-tenant login using the *original* Host header (see apps/server/src/lib/tenant.ts) —
# rewriting it would let one tenant's users log in through another tenant's hostname,
# or break login entirely. Caddy's reverse_proxy preserves Host by default; the
# `header_up Host {host}` line below is just making that explicit.
#
# To onboard a new tenant:
#   1. Client points mail.<their-domain> (CNAME or A record) at this server's IP.
#   2. Add a domain block below, importing the shared `webmail` snippet.
#   3. sudo systemctl reload caddy
# No application deploy or restart needed — the backend already accepts any
# Host header whose domain (after stripping "mail.") matches a real IMAP user.

(webmail) {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3001 {
		header_up Host {host}
	}
}

mail.jadiweb.id {
	import webmail
}

